WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.179 --> 00:00:04.569
So we've now confirmed not just the dates,
but also the moderators and the locations

00:00:04.569 --> 00:00:09.060
of the upcoming three presidential debates
and the one vice presidential debate.

00:00:09.060 --> 00:00:14.420
And Joe Biden is demanding live fact checking
during the debates, which obviously Donald

00:00:14.420 --> 00:00:16.590
Trump will oppose.

00:00:16.590 --> 00:00:19.140
But we're going to get to that in a minute.

00:00:19.140 --> 00:00:23.590
There's still some debate over whether one
or both of the candidates are going to back

00:00:23.590 --> 00:00:24.590
out.

00:00:24.590 --> 00:00:29.390
You have some Trump ists saying Biden is going
to find a way out that Biden cognitively can't

00:00:29.390 --> 00:00:30.390
do it.

00:00:30.390 --> 00:00:34.640
He would be crushed by Trump's incredible
intellect and cognitive abilities.

00:00:34.640 --> 00:00:36.399
And that Biden will find some way out.

00:00:36.399 --> 00:00:40.030
He'll say a few days before the event that
he is Cauvin or something like that.

00:00:40.030 --> 00:00:41.670
I don't think that that's going to happen.

00:00:41.670 --> 00:00:46.590
I think Biden very much understands that not
debating would not be particularly good for

00:00:46.590 --> 00:00:47.590
him.

00:00:47.590 --> 00:00:51.399
On the other hand, there are those who think
Trump is going to try to find some way out,

00:00:51.399 --> 00:00:55.610
either because he'd be scared that he won't
be able to do to Biden what he did to Hillary

00:00:55.610 --> 00:01:00.309
Clinton in terms of kind of stalking behind
her and standing physically close in that.

00:01:00.309 --> 00:01:02.579
I think that they're probably going to debate.

00:01:02.579 --> 00:01:08.530
If I had to bet now the debates are going
to be on FOX News, C-SPAN and NBC.

00:01:08.530 --> 00:01:13.470
CNN shut out of the debates for the first
time since 2008.

00:01:13.470 --> 00:01:17.900
Looking at the details, September twenty ninth,
Chris Wallace will moderate a debate on Fox

00:01:17.900 --> 00:01:20.280
News in Cleveland, Ohio.

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:25.080
It will have six, 15 minute segments with
two minutes per question.

00:01:25.080 --> 00:01:27.320
We're going to get to that in a moment.

00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:30.680
On October 7th, there will be a V.P. debate.

00:01:30.680 --> 00:01:34.540
Susan Page from USA Today will be moderating
it.

00:01:34.540 --> 00:01:37.119
It'll be at the University of Utah in Salt
Lake City.

00:01:37.119 --> 00:01:42.009
It will be nine, 10 minute segments, two minutes
per question.

00:01:42.009 --> 00:01:44.600
The second presidential will be on October
15th.

00:01:44.600 --> 00:01:48.229
Steve Scully from C-SPAN will do it in Miami,
Florida.

00:01:48.229 --> 00:01:52.939
It'll be a town minute format with two minutes
per question, with an additional minute as

00:01:52.939 --> 00:01:54.220
needed.

00:01:54.220 --> 00:01:59.159
And then lastly, the third debate will be
moderated by Kristen Welker of NBC on October

00:01:59.159 --> 00:02:00.159
22nd.

00:02:00.159 --> 00:02:02.189
That's very close to voting day.

00:02:02.189 --> 00:02:04.230
Same format as the first debate.

00:02:04.230 --> 00:02:05.299
So a few thoughts.

00:02:05.299 --> 00:02:08.509
First of all, the format favors Donald Trump.

00:02:08.509 --> 00:02:11.079
Anything shorter favors Trump.

00:02:11.079 --> 00:02:14.579
And you really can't do anything in two or
three minutes.

00:02:14.579 --> 00:02:20.299
I mean, the issues that these individuals
are dealing with are complex issues where

00:02:20.299 --> 00:02:24.219
if you had a deep understanding of them, you
would want three to four minutes just to lay

00:02:24.219 --> 00:02:25.930
layout that you understand the issue.

00:02:25.930 --> 00:02:28.510
That's how you would have serious conversation.

00:02:28.510 --> 00:02:32.109
These debates are not set up for information
purposes.

00:02:32.109 --> 00:02:36.499
These debates are shut setup for entertainment
purposes.

00:02:36.499 --> 00:02:41.299
And the shorter it is, the more it favors
Donald Trump, because I believe it's clear.

00:02:41.299 --> 00:02:45.400
Joe Biden is the one able to go deeper in
terms of policy than Donald Trump.

00:02:45.400 --> 00:02:46.400
So that's number one.

00:02:46.400 --> 00:02:52.790
Now, number two, the late debates the Trump
administration has been trying to push or

00:02:52.790 --> 00:02:57.969
the Trump campaign for an additional debate
early this month because they recognize the

00:02:57.969 --> 00:03:04.239
more people vote early, the fewer people left
to convince will be remaining on October 22nd.

00:03:04.239 --> 00:03:05.279
And that's true.

00:03:05.279 --> 00:03:11.650
I do think that on October 22nd, you're going
to have a smaller portion of the electorate,

00:03:11.650 --> 00:03:16.400
arguably, than in any prior election due to
early voting and expanded absentee ballot

00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:17.750
access.

00:03:17.750 --> 00:03:24.069
That probably is good for Joe Biden in the
sense that it's Trump who is likely to pull

00:03:24.069 --> 00:03:26.519
some kind of October surprise.

00:03:26.519 --> 00:03:30.239
And the more people that have already sent
in their ballots or voted early, whenever

00:03:30.239 --> 00:03:34.260
Trump pulls it, the less effective it's going
to be for him.

00:03:34.260 --> 00:03:39.439
Now, on the fact checking, Biden previously
said he wants some kind of live fact checking

00:03:39.439 --> 00:03:41.959
of the president on screen.

00:03:41.959 --> 00:03:43.379
Trump's obviously against that.

00:03:43.379 --> 00:03:45.139
It doesn't seem like it's going to happen.

00:03:45.139 --> 00:03:49.319
And so it's going to be up to Joe Biden to
do the fact checking.

00:03:49.319 --> 00:03:52.090
I don't need debates this year, I've said.

00:03:52.090 --> 00:03:55.930
It's never been clearer to me who we should
be supporting.

00:03:55.930 --> 00:04:00.659
But for those who want to see debates and
again, they'll be entertaining.

00:04:00.659 --> 00:04:03.439
I don't think they'll be super informative.

00:04:03.439 --> 00:04:09.839
We will be doing live streams of all for the
three presidential and the one V.P. debate.

00:04:09.839 --> 00:04:14.879
I think the V.P. debate, Kamala Harris, is
just going to eat Mike Pence up and spit them

00:04:14.879 --> 00:04:15.879
out.

00:04:15.879 --> 00:04:18.979
I just don't see any way in which Pence gets
through it unscathed.

00:04:18.979 --> 00:04:19.979
Unscathed.

00:04:19.979 --> 00:04:21.630
His followers won't care.

00:04:21.630 --> 00:04:22.630
They'll refuse to acknowledge it.

00:04:22.630 --> 00:04:24.000
But I think is going to be very, very bad
for Mike Pence.

